        "comments": "Leishmania major SD 75.1 is a strain of Leishmania, a genus of Trypanosomatid protozoa. It is associated with zoonotic cutaneous leishmaniasis, and it is spread through sandflies. Their primary hosts are vertebrates; Leishmania commonly infects canids, rodents, and humans. Leishmania currently affects 12 million people in 88 countries.\n\nThe assembly consists of 454 fragment reads (22X), three kilobase paired end reads (21X), and eight kilobase paired end reads (9X). The reads were assembled with Newbler, and then the assembly was manually improved. A contig N50 of 89K, and a scaffold N50 of 1020K was achieved.",
